<title>NEW ZEALAND: Telecom NZ, Saturn to sign interconnect deal - source.</title>
<headline>Telecom NZ, Saturn to sign interconnect deal - source.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1997-06-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Telecom Corp of New Zealand and cable TV company Saturn are expected to sign an interconnect agreement on Friday, according to information obtained by Reuters on Thursday.</p>
<p>Saturn, formerly Kiwi Cable, is controlled UIH Asia/Pacific Communications Inc, a unit United International Holdings Inc.</p>
<p>Top executives from UIH are expected in Wellington for a meeting with Telecom executives on Friday.</p>
